---
id: org.dxos.ui.react-ui-canvas
name: SceneEditor
version: 0.2.0
---

The scene editor: one editor for 2D drawings and 3D scenes over one data structure, `@dxos/scene`. Its parts —
the viewport frame, the tool rail, the actions bar, the camera bar, the display panel, the context menu, the notice,
the timeline and the docked inspector — and its behaviour — selection, tools, commands, undo and redo, the clipboard,
snapping, the lock and roles — are written once here and configured per dimension by a `DimensionConfig`. Only the
viewport and the geometry that truly differs come from the dimension. Each dimension's variant spec refers to this
one by id and states only what it adds.

The editor is react-ui-canvas-editor, the application; react-ui-canvas is the surface it draws on in either dimension:
the 2D engine, the 3D renderer, the read-only views, the element kinds and the headless rules. The editor owns no
model. The document changes only through `LayoutIntent`s and `ModelIntent`s ([org.dxos.scene#F-1.7]); a viewport
draws the document, picks, and reports gestures as intents and selection changes, and never writes the document or
owns a command.

Requirements marked **(planned)** are designed and not built. Requirement ids start at F-10: the ids below it name
the engine requirements the 2D variant states.

## Dependencies

```mdl
uses org.dxos.scene: The data the editor edits — Model, Layout, Scene, the element base, styles and catalogs, composites and the intent vocabulary — which this spec refers to and does not restate.
```

## Ontology

| Term                 | Definition                                                                                                                                                       |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Document**         | A `SceneDocument`: the Models, Layouts and Scenes of one canvas (`org.dxos.scene`).                                                                              |
| **Open scene**       | The one Scene of the document a viewer shows, kept by key in the canvas's view state.                                                                            |
| **Open layout**      | The layout being edited: the open scene's own, or a composite's parts when the viewer has drilled into it.                                                       |
| **Element**          | An item of a layout, shape or link alike (`type:BaseElement`); a link is an element with endpoints.                                                              |
| **Object**           | A reusable model object an element places; a **composite** is one whose `parts` is a layout in local units, placed through the element's transform.             |
| **Style**            | A named look an element references by `style`, overridden per element by `overrides`; `Style2D` in 2D, `Style3D` in 3D, resolved through **catalogs**.          |
| **Look**             | A theme: the default style catalog of a dimension, picked in the display panel.                                                                                  |
| **Dimension config** | What one dimension supplies to the editor: its viewport, tools, geometry, camera maths, display options, property form, sections and commands.                  |
| **Picture**          | The editor drawn with no chrome: the authored view of the open scene, in a card, section or slide.                                                               |
| **Shot**             | An animator shot staging the open scene: a timeline sampled into the viewport, never written to the document.                                                   |

## Extensions

| Term        | URI                          |
| ----------- | ---------------------------- |
| `uses`      | `dxos.spec.core/uses`        |
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
