## Types

The document's types are `org.dxos.scene`'s. These are the editor's own: the extension points a dimension fills,
and the state every part reads.

```mdl
type DimensionConfig
  desc: >
    Everything one dimension gives the editor; the rest is the editor's own. `C` is the dimension's camera.
  fields:
    dim: '2d' | '3d'
    viewport: Component<ViewportProps<C>>
    tools: ToolDef[]                  # the rail, grouped by category and group
    toolDragData?: (tool) => data     # what dragging a rail tool onto the viewport drops (2D: a node of its type)
    geometry: GeometryOps
    camera: CameraOps<C>
    display: DisplayOptions
    propertyForm: Component<PropertyFormProps>    # `createPropertyForm` builds one from a schema
    propertyFormSelection?: boolean   # the form edits a whole selection, not one element
    propertyInfo?: (state: { face? }) => node     # a line over the form (3D: the selected face)
    sections?: SectionDef[]           # the dimension's own inspector sections, after the shared ones
    animatable?: AnimatableFields     # the element fields the Timeline keys; `placementFields` when unset
    commands?: ExtraCommandDef[]      # commands only this dimension offers
```

```mdl
type ToolDef
  desc: >
    One tool on the rail. Its category decides its rail group and whether a locked editor keeps it: only `select`
    tools (Select and the hand) stay when locked.
  fields:
    id: string
    icon: string
    label: string
    category: 'select' | 'transform' | 'create'
    kind?: string                     # a create tool's element type
    key?: string                      # its shortcut
    group?: string                    # its rail group; the category's group when unset
```

```mdl
type ViewportProps
  desc: >
    What the editor gives the dimension's viewport, and the only ways the viewport reports back. The viewport draws
    the document as stored (or as the Timeline samples it), runs a gesture in memory, and reports the gesture's end as
    one intent.
  fields:
    document: SceneDocument
    scene: string
    editing?: string                  # the open layout; the scene's own when unset
    selection: string[]
    tool: ActiveTool
    readonly: boolean
    picture?: boolean                 # the authored view only: no gestures, grid, axes, guides or chrome
    grid, snap: boolean
    axes?, guides?: boolean
    theme: string                     # the look: a default style catalog
    face?: FaceSelection
    camera?: C                        # this viewer's camera
    onSelect: (ids) => void
    onToolChange?: (tool) => void     # the viewport changed the tool (a create tool giving way to select)
    onIntent: (layout, intent: LayoutIntent) => void
    onModelIntent?: (intent: ModelIntent) => problems
    onTransaction?: (change) => void  # the intents `change` writes are one undo step
    onPreview: (layout?, intent?) => void         # an in-flight gesture, drawn and not written
    path?: string[]                   # the drill path to the open layout from the scene's own; empty at the scene's own
    onEdit: (path) => void            # open a level of the drill path: deeper to drill in, shorter to drill out
    onContextMenu: (at, kind: 'element' | 'canvas') => void
    onFaceChange?, onCameraChange?, onResize?
    children?: node                   # the floating panels, drawn over the scene
```

```mdl
type GeometryOps
  desc: Moving and snapping in the dimension's units.
  fields:
    pasteOffset: (pasted: number) => Vec    # how far the n-th paste of one copy lands from it
    snap: { move: number, rotate?: number, scale?: number }
```

```mdl
type CameraOps
  desc: The camera bar's maths over the dimension's camera.
  fields:
    fit: (camera, document, layout, size) => C        # frame the open layout's elements
    reset: (authored, document, layout, size) => C    # actual size: the authored camera's scale, centred on the content
    zoom: (camera, factor) => C
    percent: (camera, authored) => number             # the zoom against the authored camera's
```

```mdl
type DisplayOptions
  desc: What the display panel offers.
  fields:
    themes: { id, label }[]           # the looks, each a default style catalog
    grids: GridKind[]
    guides: boolean                   # whether the dimension has guides at all
```

```mdl
type EditorDisplay
  desc: >
    A viewer's display choices: view state, never the document. The look's override is the viewer's; the drawing's
    own theme is shared.
  fields:
    theme: string
    themeOverride?: string
    grid: boolean
    snap: boolean
    guides: boolean
    axes?: boolean
```

```mdl
type EditorStore
  desc: >
    The editor's state as atoms, which every part reads: view state, never the document. It lives as long as the
    editor (a strict-mode remount reuses it).
  fields:
    selection: string[]               # element ids of the open layout, links included
    tool: ActiveTool                  # { id, object? }: `place` carries the model object it places
    editing: string[]                 # the drill path from the scene's own layout; empty at the scene's own
    face?: FaceSelection              # 3D only: an element and the normal of the side picked
    preview?: EditorPreview           # an in-flight gesture's intent, drawn and not written
    menu?: MenuAnchor                 # where the context menu opened, over an element or empty space
    notice?: string                   # the last command's message (a refused paste, a failed import)
    shot?, time, playing              # the Timeline's shot, playhead and play state
```

```mdl
type CommandTable
  desc: >
    The editor's commands as every surface shows and runs them: the actions bar, the context menu, the shortcuts and
    the app. Built by `buildCommands` from the shared commands and the dimension's extras.
  fields:
    commands: Command[]               # { id, label, icon, shortcut?, enabled, run }
    get: (id) => Command
    menuItems: (kind: 'element' | 'canvas') => MenuItem[]
    keyCommand: (event) => Command    # the command a chord runs
```

```mdl
type ExtraCommandDef
  desc: >
    A command only one dimension offers. It reads the open layout and the selection and edits through intents, like
    the shared commands; `import` is offered by the Objects section rather than the actions bar.
  fields:
    id: string
    label: string
    icon: string
    enabled: (state: { selection, readonly }) => boolean
    run: (context: { document, layout, selection, onIntent, onModelIntent, select, setTool, notify }) => void
```

```mdl
type History
  desc: >
    Undo and redo over a canvas. A layout step is field-level inverse patches between the source's heads before and
    after it; a model edit (group, ungroup, make object) is a document step, undone by writing back the document
    before it. `sessionHistory(canvas)` keeps the steps for the session.
  fields:
    record: (change) => void          # the writes `change` makes are one step
    recordDocument: (before, after) => void
    undo, redo: () => void
    state: { canUndo, canRedo }
```

```mdl
type ClipboardCodec
  desc: The `.dx` text a copy writes and a paste reads, lifted or flattened into the dimension pasted into.
  fields:
    write: (document, layout, fragment) => string
    read: (text, dim) => Fragment
```

```mdl
type EditorShot
  desc: A shot the Timeline lists: an animator shot staging the open scene, with its timeline.
  fields:
    id: string
    name?: string
    timeline: Timeline                # `@dxos/animation`
```

## Components

The editor is one composite, `SceneEditor`. `Root` holds the store, the command table, the history, the clipboard,
the lock and the role; every other part reads them through `useSceneEditor` and is placed by the host, so a host
may leave a part out or move it.

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Root
  desc: >
    The shared editor for one canvas: the dimension's config, the document and the open scene, and the host's
    writers. Inside a card, section or slide it draws the viewport alone, as a picture. Wraps its writes in the
    history, so every edit a part or the viewport makes is recorded once.
  props:
    config: DimensionConfig
    document: SceneDocument
    scene: string
    role?: string                     # the surface role; only an article edits
    readonly?: boolean                # the lock
    onReadonlyChange?
    onIntent: (layout, intent) => void
    onModelIntent?: (intent) => problems
    readDocument?: () => SceneDocument            # either side of a model edit, for its undo step
    history?: History
    onLayersChange?
    codec?: ClipboardCodec
    display: EditorDisplay
    onDisplayChange?
    camera?: C                        # this viewer's camera, unset until they move it
    authoredCamera?: C                # the scene's own
    onCameraChange?
    refitKey?: string | number        # a new key frames the open layout's content (an agent's edit asks for it)
    docked?: boolean
    onDockedChange?
    sceneChoice?: SceneChoice         # the open scene, and adding and deleting scenes
    shots?: EditorShot[]
    onShotChange?: (shot?, timeline) => void
    timeline?: boolean                # the Timeline shown; the editor's own choice when `onTimelineChange` is unset
    onTimelineChange?
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Viewport
  desc: >
    The dimension's viewport in the shared frame with the inspector panel (`InspectorPanel.Frame`); its children are
    the floating panels drawn over it.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Navigation
  desc: >
    The breadcrumbs (`NavigationToolbar`), top left: Up, then the drill path from the scene's own layout (named by the
    scene) to the open layout. A crumb opens that level; Up opens the one above.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Tools
  desc: >
    The tool rail (`ToolRail`), left below the breadcrumbs: the config's tools by group in the order they first appear — the select
    tools, the transform tools, then the create group, which folds into a flyout when the rail is short — with the
    lock toggle at the end of the select group. Locked, only the select tools stay. A tool with drag data drags onto
    the viewport.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Actions
  desc: The actions bar, bottom centre: the command table's commands. Locked, it hides, as every one edits but Copy.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Camera
  desc: >
    The camera bar, bottom left: fit, actual size, zoom in and out by 1.25, and the zoom as a percentage of the
    authored camera's. It moves only this viewer's camera, never the scene's.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Display
  desc: >
    The display panel (`DisplayPanel`), bottom right: the look (each theme with its swatch and a sun or moon for its
    mode), the grid, snapping, the axes toggle (its icon by dimension: `vector-two` in 2D, `vector-three` in 3D),
    where the dimension has them guides, and, where the host has shots, the Timeline toggle.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.ContextMenu
  desc: The right-click menu (`SceneContextMenu`): the command table's items over an element or empty space.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Notice
  desc: The last command's message, such as a refused paste or a failed import.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Timeline
  desc: >
    The Timeline panel, above the actions bar, hidden until the display panel's Timeline toggle shows it: the shots
    staging the open scene (a picker when there are several), a play button and a playhead, and a key button that keys
    the selection's animatable fields at the playhead.
```

```mdl
component SceneEditor.Inspector
  desc: >
    The one inspector panel (`InspectorPanel`), docked beside the viewport or floating over it, with the dock toggle
    on its toolbar. Its sections stack in order — Properties, Views, Objects, Layers, Styles — then the dimension's
    own; docked, Properties fills the upper half above the rest, split by a seam that can be dragged.
  slots:
    Properties: the config's form over the selection, shown as drawn (its object's size, type and look applied)
    Views: the scene's layout tree (`ViewsInspector`), with a composite's parts read-only under the element placing it
    Objects: the model's objects (`ObjectsInspector`), each with how many elements place it
    Layers: the open layout's layers (`LayersInspector`)
    Styles: the drawing's named styles, then the catalogs' (`StylesInspector`)
```

```mdl
component GeometryField
  desc: >
    A vector field and an optional companion vector side by side in two columns (`makeGeometryField`), the
    companion's own row hidden: 2D draws centre and size, 3D centre and scale. Shared so both Properties forms lay out
    vectors alike.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-10: One editor, configured per dimension
  req F-10.1: Both dimensions render `SceneEditor` over the same document types; the dimension's `DimensionConfig`
    supplies the viewport, tools, geometry, camera maths, display options, property form, sections, animatable fields
    and extra commands, and nothing else differs.
  req F-10.2: A part reads the editor's state through `useSceneEditor`, with `useEditorSelection` and
    `useEditorCommands` for the selection and the command table.
  req F-10.3: (planned) The editor's context is split by aspect with one hook per aspect, as the 2D engine's `Canvas`
    has (document, tools, look, navigation, editing); panels and inspectors read those hooks, and each config supplies
    its implementations behind them.
  req F-10.4: Each viewer opens one of the canvas's scenes, kept by key in the canvas's view state; the Views section
    picks, adds and deletes scenes the same way in both dimensions, keeping the last ([org.dxos.scene#D-84]).
```

```mdl
feat F-11: Edits are intents
  req F-11.1: A gesture — drag, resize, rotate, orbit, drag-to-create — runs in memory and commits one intent on
    release, in both dimensions; while it runs, the in-flight intent is the store's `preview`, drawn and not written.
  req F-11.2: The editor writes a layout only through `onIntent` and a model only through `onModelIntent`; a model
    edit's problems refuse it and are shown as the notice.
  req F-11.3: The intents one change writes across layouts and the model (a new portal: its element, its layout and
    its object) are one undo step (`onTransaction`).
  req F-11.4: A plugin's element kind extends the element base and registers in the kind registry; a layout keeps a
    kind's own fields, which the registry validates ([org.dxos.scene#D-93]).
```

```mdl
feat F-12: Selection and tools
  req F-12.1: Elements and links are selected together in one set of ids of the open layout; Delete removes the
    selection (the viewport's own key, since it knows a face from an element).
  req F-12.2: The rail groups tools alike in both dimensions: the select tools (Select, the hand), the transform
    tools, then one create group of the shapes followed by Link ([org.dxos.scene#D-79]).
  req F-12.3: With a create tool, a click or Shift-click on an element selects or toggles it as Select does, so a
    create tool makes an element only on empty space ([org.dxos.scene#D-80]).
  req F-12.4: Holding Cmd turns a left drag into the hand in both dimensions, its cursor shown while the key is held
    ([org.dxos.scene#D-77]).
  req F-12.5: Drilling into a composite makes its parts the open layout, and Escape drills back out; each variant
    says which gesture drills. The breadcrumbs show the drill path in both dimensions, and a crumb drills out to its
    level.
  req F-12.6: Placing a model object is the `place` tool carrying that object; an object is never placed inside its
    own parts ([org.dxos.scene#D-49]).
```

```mdl
feat F-13: Commands and the context menu
  req F-13.1: One command table serves the actions bar, the context menu, the shortcuts and the app: Cut, Copy,
    Paste, Duplicate, Group, Ungroup, Make object, Delete, Undo and Redo, then the dimension's extras.
  req F-13.2: Right-clicking the view or a selection opens the shared menu with the commands that apply there and
    their shortcuts; a right-click on an unselected element selects it first ([org.dxos.scene#D-81]).
  req F-13.3: Cmd/Ctrl+D duplicates the selection one paste step aside in both dimensions ([org.dxos.scene#D-72]).
  req F-13.4: The shortcuts work on the whole window while the last press was inside the editor, so they still work
    after a clicked control drops focus to the page; typing in a field keeps its own keys. A press inside the
    editor focuses it, in either dimension.
```

```mdl
feat F-14: Undo and the clipboard
  req F-14.1: Every edit is one undo step, recorded by the root: a layout edit as field-level inverse patches, a
    model edit as the document before and after it.
  req F-14.2: Undo writes a field back only while it still holds the value the step wrote; a field a peer changed
    since is skipped ([org.dxos.scene#D-63]).
  req F-14.3: A canvas's history lasts for the session: it survives closing and reopening the editor and is not
    persisted ([org.dxos.scene#D-63]).
  req F-14.4: A copy keeps the selection as the session's clipboard, shared by every editor, and writes it to the
    system clipboard as `.dx` text with every placed object folded in ([org.dxos.scene#D-69]).
  req F-14.5: A paste pastes the session's copy again, one paste step further each time, while the system clipboard
    still holds its text; otherwise it reads the system clipboard's `.dx` text into the dimension, lifting 2D onto
    the ground or flattening 3D to its top-down view ([org.dxos.scene#D-62]). Pasted elements get fresh ids, and a
    paste that would place an object inside its own parts is refused.
```

```mdl
feat F-15: Display, snapping and axes
  req F-15.1: The display panel's choices are the viewer's view state: the look (a default style catalog), the grid,
    snapping, the axes and the dimension's guides.
  req F-15.2: Snapping moves, turns and scales by the config's steps; holding Alt frees one gesture.
  req F-15.3: The axes toggle shows the axes through the origin whenever it is on, read-only included; a picture
    draws none.
  req F-15.4: A picture draws no grid, snapping, axes or guides ([org.dxos.scene#D-55]).
  req F-15.5: A picture draws the authored view framed to fit, never the viewer's own camera.
  req F-15.6: The Timeline is hidden until the viewer shows it from the display panel.
```

```mdl
feat F-16: The lock and roles
  req F-16.1: Only the article edits a scene (the role `article`, a namespaced `….article`, or no role); a card,
    section or slide draws the viewport alone as a picture of the authored view, with no chrome.
  req F-16.2: One read-only lock per canvas, shared by both dimensions and toggled on the rail; locked, only the
    select tools, the camera and Copy work, and the actions bar hides ([org.dxos.scene#D-59]).
```

```mdl
feat F-17: Camera
  req F-17.1: The camera bar moves this viewer's camera, never the scene's authored camera
    ([org.dxos.scene#D-47]).
  req F-17.2: Fit frames the open layout's elements; actual size takes the authored camera's scale, centred on the
    content; zoom steps by 1.25; the readout is the zoom as a percentage of the authored camera's.
  req F-17.3: A new `refitKey` frames the open layout's content even after the viewer moved the camera, so an
    agent's edit can bring its result into view.
```

```mdl
feat F-18: Panels and inspectors
  req F-18.1: The panels float over the viewport in the same places in both dimensions: the breadcrumbs top left,
    the rail at the left below them, the actions bar at the bottom centre with the Timeline above it, the camera bar bottom left, the display panel bottom
    right.
  req F-18.2: One inspector panel serves both dimensions and docks in both; the dock choice is the canvas's view
    state, so it holds in either dimension ([org.dxos.scene#D-66]).
  req F-18.3: The sections are Properties, Views, Objects, Layers and Styles, in that order, then the dimension's
    own; Properties goes while nothing is selected.
  req F-18.4: Properties edits the selection through intents with the config's form; a typed value commits once,
    on blur or Enter, and Escape puts the saved value back; steppers, pickers and toggles commit at once
    ([org.dxos.scene#D-73]).
  req F-18.5: Views shows the open scene's layout tree, each element under it and a composite's parts read-only
    under the element placing it; a row selects, and a composite row drills in.
  req F-18.6: Objects lists the model's objects with how many elements place each; it places one with the place
    tool, opens a composite's parts, and makes an object of the selection.
  req F-18.7: Layers lists the open layout's layers, bottom first; a hidden layer's elements are neither drawn nor
    picked, nor the links bound to them.
```

```mdl
feat F-19: Styles
  req F-19.1: An element names a style by `style` and carries its own `overrides`; its look resolves nearest first,
    field by field: overrides, the layout's override of the style, the model's definition, each catalog in order,
    then the look's default catalog ([org.dxos.scene#D-92]).
  req F-19.2: The Styles section lists the drawing's named styles, then each catalog's (read-only); clicking one
    sets the selection's `style`.
  req F-19.3: A new style takes the selected element's own look (its overrides) into the model under the first free
    `style-n` key and points the element at it.
  req F-19.4: The display panel's look picks the default catalog in both dimensions.
```

```mdl
feat F-20: Composites
  req F-20.1: A composite is a model object whose parts layout is in local units, placed by an element that
    carries its transform; editing its parts is drilling into that layout.
  req F-20.2: Group makes an anonymous composite of the selection placed by one element; Ungroup puts its parts
    back; Make object makes a named model object of the selection; each is one undo step.
```

```mdl
feat F-21: Animation
  req F-21.1: The Timeline panel lists the shots staging the open scene and plays or scrubs one by sampling it into
    the viewport; the document is never written.
  req F-21.2: Keying writes the selection's animatable fields at the playhead into the shot's timeline; with no shot,
    the first key makes one.
  req F-21.3: (planned) The Timeline keys the camera as well as the selected elements.
```

## Rules

Conventions this package's code must hold that a linter cannot express; each block is discovered by the
agentic-review harness.

```mdl
rule editor-writes-through-intents: The editor changes the document only through its intent writers
  Every change the editor or a viewport makes to the document leaves through `onIntent`, `onModelIntent` or
  `onTransaction`. Code under react-ui-canvas-editor's `src/editor` must not write an ECHO object, a layout record or
  a document field directly, and a viewport must not own a command: commands are the command table's. Flag a write to
  a document, layout, model or ECHO object in that code that does not go through those writers.
  scope: repo
  files:
    - packages/ui/react-ui-canvas-editor/src/editor/**/*.ts
    - packages/ui/react-ui-canvas-editor/src/editor/**/*.tsx
  severity: error
```

```mdl
rule named-react-imports: Import React members by name, never through a `React.` namespace
  Use `import { useMemo, type Ref } from 'react'` and call `useMemo(...)`; do not write
  `React.useMemo`, `React.FC`, `React.ReactNode` or `import React from 'react'`. A forwarded ref is
  named `forwardedRef`. Flag any `React.` member access and any default import of react in the
  source of react-ui-canvas or react-ui-canvas-editor. Do not flag `import type * as React from 'react'`
  used solely in a `.d.ts` ambient declaration.
  scope: repo
  files:
    - packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/**/*.tsx
    - packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/**/*.ts
    - packages/ui/react-ui-canvas-editor/src/**/*.tsx
    - packages/ui/react-ui-canvas-editor/src/**/*.ts
  grep: React\.|import React
  severity: warn
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The engine's containers are Views, Objects and Tags, as the Ontology defines them; scene, frame, composite and layer are no longer container terms, and this spec is the one current model.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [View, Tag, Layer, BuiltinNode, F-9]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Tags and container order are specified now and marked planned, beside the `Layer` type and [F-3.15] that describe what is built. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Tag, Layer, F-3.15, F-9.6, F-9.7]
  why: The design is settled and the review can then report the gap as missing work, while the built behaviour stays specified until it changes.
  rejected:
    - Leaving tags and order out until built, which keeps the design in a second document.
    - Describing only tags, which leaves layers unspecified while they are what the code does.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Undo is a log of field-level patches between store heads, one entry per committed edit and one log per canvas document, recorded on Composer's `HistoryTracker` when the host has one; projections expose their own model instead of snapshots. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Projection, CanvasHistory, F-4.1, F-4.2, F-4.4, F-4.5, F-4.6, T-5]
  why: The snapshot log the spec described was removed when undo moved to patches; the spec follows the code, whose decisions are in the canvas-views design.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Group, Ungroup, library promotion and orphan pruning move from [F-3.13] to [F-9.2]–[F-9.5], and `frame` reading as `view` is [F-9.1]. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.13, F-9]
  why: They are the container model's behaviour, not selection editing.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: An Object cannot contain a View. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-9.9]
  why: An Object is drawn at every placement and opened only in isolation; a View inside it would be a navigable place repeated per Instance, with no single drill path.
  rejected:
    - Allowing it, which the design left open and nothing built needs.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Approve [D-2], [D-3], [D-4] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A stored `frame` node is read as `view`, and the next write stores it as `view`.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-9.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Group refuses a selection holding a `view` node, and creating or pasting a `view` node into an Object's definition is refused, so no View ends up inside an Object.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-9.9]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: F-3.15 points at the tags requirement [F-9.6] and the container-order requirement [F-9.7] as its successors.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.15]
```

```mdl
decision D-10: 2D and 3D share one data structure, with variance only where it is required, and one editor with common panels, with variance, that each dimension configures separately.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10, DimensionConfig]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The shared editor has common components (panels, inspectors, the canvas, the context menu), common behaviours (cut, copy, paste, undo, redo, selection, the lock and roles) and pluggable behaviours only where the dimensions truly differ.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10, F-12, F-13, F-14, F-16, F-18]
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The editor lives in react-ui-canvas under its current name; "canvas" is the surface in either dimension.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root]
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Every feature is designed for both dimensions first, in shared behaviour and shared implementation; only the viewport and the dimension-specific geometry differ.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10, DimensionConfig]
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Gestures stay in memory while they run (drag, resize, rotate, orbit, drag-to-create) and commit one intent on release, in both dimensions, so editing is smooth on ECHO.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-11.1, EditorStore]
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Styles have one term, Style, with typed variants that are not conflated: `Style2D` (CSS-like) and `Style3D` (material-like). There is one mechanism: named styles defined in the model, overridden by layouts, referenced by elements by id with per-element overrides, and resolved through shared style catalogs, custom catalogs being ECHO objects and themes the default catalogs.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-19]
```

```mdl
decision D-16: The element schema is re-based on react-ui-canvas's schema, keeping its field names and shapes (`type`, `z`, `source`/`target` endpoints, ports, points). Only what was decided changes: one element type for nodes and links, a link being an element with endpoints; a named `style` reference (the canvas's `class`) plus `overrides` (its inline `style`), with `Style2D`/`Style3D` and catalogs; and the Model/Layout/Scene split. `Element3D` shares the same base, and `@dxos/scene`'s `kind`, `order`, `from`/`to` bindings, `members` and shared style tokens are replaced with no aliases.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10.1, F-11.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-17: Plugin-defined kinds extend the element schema as they extend the canvas's node schema today and register in the kind registry; a layout's elements store validates the shared base and keeps unknown fields, and the registry validates each kind's own fields.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-11.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-18: There is one animation system: `@dxos/animation`'s `Timeline`, owned by plugin-animator's shots, is the only timeline model, and react-ui-canvas's own timeline is retired. A shared Timeline panel in the editor, in 2D and 3D, lists and plays the shots staging the open scene, keyframes the selected elements and the camera, and creates a shot when none exists.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-21, SceneEditor.Timeline]
```

```mdl
decision D-19: Composite objects have relative positioning in both dimensions: a composite is a model object whose parts layout is in local units, and the element that places it carries the transform (object, centre, scale, rotation, and fit `none` or `frame`). Parts draw at the centre plus the rotated, scaled local position, with strokes and text scaled too. Diagram objects become composites placed by elements, 3D groups use the same mechanism, and the SVG renderer and both viewports draw parts through the transform.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-20]
```

```mdl
decision D-20: The display panel has a toggle that shows the axes, in both dimensions.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Display, F-15.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-21: The axes show whenever the toggle is on, read-only included.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-15.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-22: The axes toggle's icon is `vector-two` in 2D and `vector-three` in 3D.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Display]
```

```mdl
decision D-23: The shared editor has the structure of the 2D engine's `Canvas`: `SceneEditor.Root` provides one shared context split by aspect with a hook per aspect, the panels and inspectors are composite parts that read those hooks, and each dimension's config supplies its implementations behind the same hooks.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-24: The core states only what both dimensions share. The engine's navigation through portals, its grid lattice and guides, ports and links, its View model and intents, the 2D Properties form and 2D styles are the 2D variant's; orbit, gizmos, face selection, solids, mesh import and export, materials and drag-to-create with height are the 3D variant's. The core's requirement ids start at F-10, so the engine ids the earlier entries of this log name (F-1 to F-9, T-1 to T-6) keep their meaning in the 2D variant. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10, F-11, F-12, F-13, F-14, F-15, F-16, F-17, F-18, F-19, F-20, F-21]
  why: The split follows the shared and per-dimension columns of the editor's feature table, and keeping the old ids out of the core keeps every earlier entry of this log pointing at the requirement it was made about.
  rejected:
    - Renumbering the engine's requirements from F-1 in the variant and the core alike, which would make the earlier entries name the wrong requirements.
```

```mdl
decision D-25: A dimension config supplies the viewport, tools, tool drag data, geometry (paste offset and snap steps), camera maths (fit, actual size, zoom, percent), display options (looks, grid kinds, guides), the property form (and whether it edits a whole selection, and a line above it), extra inspector sections, the animatable fields and extra commands; everything else is the editor's. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [DimensionConfig, ToolDef, ViewportProps, GeometryOps, CameraOps, DisplayOptions, F-10.1]
  why: These are exactly the places where the two editors' code differed once the shared parts were taken out.
```

```mdl
decision D-26: The editor's state is one store of atoms — selection, tool, drill path, selected face, the in-flight gesture's preview, the menu anchor, the notice, and the Timeline's shot, time and play state — which is view state and never the document. Fills in [D-14].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [EditorStore, F-11.1]
  why: A gesture's preview in the store lets every part draw the edit under way while the document receives one intent at its end.
```

```mdl
decision D-27: One command table (`buildCommands`) holds the shared commands and the dimension's extras with their enabled states, and the actions bar, the context menu, the shortcuts and the app all read it; locked, only Copy is enabled. The shortcuts listen on the whole window while the last press was inside the editor, and a press inside focuses it. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [CommandTable, ExtraCommandDef, F-13]
  why: A focus-only listener lost the shortcuts as soon as a clicked panel control took focus, and the 3D view takes no focus of its own.
```

```mdl
decision D-28: The editor's history keeps a layout edit as field-level inverse patches and a model edit as the documents before and after it, both in the canvas's session history; the root records every write, and a change spanning several writers is one step. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [History, F-11.3, F-14.1, F-14.2, F-14.3]
  why: Patches undo a layout edit without overwriting a peer's later edit to another field; a model edit touches objects and layouts together, which only a document step restores as one.
```

```mdl
decision D-29: The clipboard is one session clipboard shared by every editor, mirrored to the system clipboard as `.dx` text through a codec that lifts or flattens across dimensions; a repeated paste steps by the dimension's paste offset. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [ClipboardCodec, F-14.4, F-14.5]
  why: A copy in one canvas then pastes into another of either dimension, into documents and to the assistant.
```

```mdl
decision D-30: The camera bar's actual size takes the authored camera's scale centred on the open layout's content in both dimensions, its zoom steps by 1.25, and a host's `refitKey` frames the content again. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [CameraOps, SceneEditor.Camera, F-17]
  why: Restoring the authored camera unchanged could leave the content out of view when the viewport's size differs from the one it was authored in.
```

```mdl
decision D-31: The panels default to the same places in both dimensions (rail left, actions bottom centre, Timeline above them, camera bottom left, display bottom right), and the inspector's sections are Properties, Views, Objects, Layers and Styles, then the dimension's own. Fills in [D-10] and [D-15].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Tools, SceneEditor.Actions, SceneEditor.Camera, SceneEditor.Display, SceneEditor.Inspector, F-18]
  why: The 2D canvas's placement was already the one people knew, and the Styles section joins the shared ones because styles work the same in both dimensions.
```

```mdl
decision D-32: The Styles section lists the drawing's named styles before the catalogs', applies a click to the selection, and makes a new style from the selected element's overrides under the first free `style-n` key. Fills in [D-15].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-19.2, F-19.3]
  why: The drawing's own styles are the ones a person edits; a catalog's are shared and read-only here.
```

```mdl
decision D-33: The Timeline panel keys the selection's animatable fields (the config's, or the placement fields) at the playhead, and samples the shot into the viewport while the playhead is off the start or playing. Keying the camera is not built and is marked planned. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [EditorShot, SceneEditor.Timeline, F-21]
  why: The spec states what the panel does now; the camera key is the part of [D-18] still to build.
```

```mdl
decision D-34: Parts read the editor through one context (`useSceneEditor`) with `useEditorSelection` and `useEditorCommands`; the split by aspect is marked planned. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-10.2, F-10.3]
  why: That is the structure built; recording the aspect split as planned keeps the gap visible rather than describing hooks that do not exist.
```

```mdl
decision D-35: Code under `src/editor` changes the document only through the intent writers, and a viewport owns no command; the `editor-writes-through-intents` rule checks it. Fills in [D-14].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [editor-writes-through-intents, F-11.2]
  why: One write path is what lets the root record every edit for undo and lets both dimensions share commands.
```

```mdl
decision D-36: Only an article edits: a card, section or slide draws the viewport as a picture of the authored view with no chrome, and the one read-only lock per canvas leaves the select tools, the camera and Copy. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-16, F-15.4]
  why: A namespaced role (`….article`) must edit as the plain one does, so the test is the role's last segment.
```

```mdl
decision D-37: Scene UI is two packages: react-ui-canvas is the surface (2D engine, 3D renderer, read-only views, element kinds, headless rules) and react-ui-canvas-editor is the editor application (SceneEditor, panels, inspectors, history, commands, timeline, the 2D and 3D configs); react-ui-scene is removed, and 2D and 3D share both packages.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  supersedes: D-12
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root, DimensionConfig]
```

```mdl
decision D-38: react-ui-canvas's root, `/headless`, `/motion`, `/generator-worker` and `/testing` entries load neither the 3D renderer nor manifold; the Babylon renderer, manifold solids and `Scene3DView` are its `/3d` entry and mesh import and export its `/io` entry, and the `/scene` entry is removed. Babylon and manifold-3d are regular dependencies of react-ui-canvas. Fills in [D-37].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root]
  why: Operations and 2D-only hosts import the root, so keeping the 3D runtime behind its own entry keeps them free of a WASM module and a large renderer they never draw with.
  rejected:
    - Exporting the renderer from the root, which loads Babylon into every 2D card and operation handler.
    - A separate 3D package, which would split the surface the decision keeps whole.
```

```mdl
decision D-39: The dependency direction is checked twice: lint forbids react-ui-canvas from importing react-ui-canvas-editor, and a react-ui-canvas test fails when a light entry reaches @babylonjs, manifold-3d or the editor through its value imports, when any source file imports the editor, or when the manifest lists it. Fills in [D-37].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root]
  why: Lint catches a direct import at the line that adds it; the test also catches a light entry that reaches the renderer through a chain of relative imports, which no import rule sees.
```

```mdl
decision D-40: The engine's own 2D chrome (its toolbar, breadcrumbs and inspector panels) is react-ui-canvas-editor's `CanvasEditor`, which frames react-ui-canvas's `Canvas.Root` through a `shell` slot; `Canvas.Root` stays in react-ui-canvas as the engine root that `Scene2DView` and the 2D viewport draw with. Fills in [D-37].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root]
  why: The engine's end-to-end suites and plugin-canvas's data-flow sample still drive that chrome, so it moves with the editor rather than being deleted.
  rejected:
    - Deleting the chrome and porting the end-to-end suites and the sample onto `SceneEditor` in the same change.
    - Leaving the chrome in react-ui-canvas, which keeps editor panels in the surface.
```

```mdl
decision D-41: `Scene2DView` draws in 2D only; a host that shows a 2D scene in 3D lifts it (`liftScene`, `camera2DTo3D`) and draws it with `Scene3DView` from the `/3d` entry. Fills in [D-38].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root]
  why: A 3D option on the 2D view would import the renderer into the root entry.
```

```mdl
decision D-42: The viewport contract (`ViewportProps`, `ActiveTool`, `FaceSelection`, `ConstrainIntent`, `ConstrainContext`) and `sampleDocument` are react-ui-canvas's, which the editor imports. Fills in [D-37].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [DimensionConfig]
  why: The surface implements the viewport contract, and operations sample a shot's document without loading the editor.
```

```mdl
decision D-43: The canvas article shows the breadcrumbs top left, as the 2D engine's own chrome did.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-18.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-44: The look menu shows each theme's snapshot and its light or dark icon.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Display]
```

```mdl
decision D-45: A frame's content is sized to the frame.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-15]
```

```mdl
decision D-46: Zooming into frames drills into them. The 2D engine's own drill-in, breadcrumbs and frame rendering are the reference: the editor matches them exactly in 2D, with parity in 3D.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-12.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-47: The animation panel is hidden by default.
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Timeline]
```

```mdl
decision D-48: The breadcrumbs are a `SceneEditor.Navigation` part over the drill path, the root crumb named by the scene; the rail moves below them. Fills in [D-43].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Navigation, SceneEditor.Tools, F-18.1]
  why: A part keeps the breadcrumbs shared by 2D and 3D and lets each host place them, as it places the other panels.
  rejected:
    - The 2D engine's own breadcrumbs: they cover 2D only and read the engine's path, not the editor's.
```

```mdl
decision D-49: The editor's drill path is the full path from the scene's own layout, empty at the scene's own; the viewport receives it as `path` and reports a level with `onEdit(path)`, so a crumb opens any level and the 2D engine follows the editor. Fills in [D-46].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [ViewportProps, EditorStore, F-12.5]
  why: Keeping only the root and the leaf lost every level between them, so the breadcrumbs could not drill out one step and the engine and the editor disagreed after a nested drill.
  rejected:
    - The engine owning the path, the editor mirroring it: 3D has no engine path.
```

```mdl
decision D-50: A picture is given no viewer camera, so it frames the authored view to fit; the 2D viewport applies a host camera only when its values change. Fills in [D-45] and [D-46].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-15.5, SceneEditor.Root]
  why: The article's own camera, pushed into a card or section after its fit, drew the content at the wrong scale, and re-pushing the same root camera pulled a drilled-in view back to the root.
```

```mdl
decision D-51: The Timeline shows when the host passes `timeline` or the display panel's film-strip toggle is on; the choice is the editor's own unless the host controls it with `onTimelineChange`. Fills in [D-47].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SceneEditor.Root, SceneEditor.Display, SceneEditor.Timeline, F-15.6]
